{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>For, your hand</b> — your blow, for a blow is by hand." "<b>Shaddai</b> — from the root לשד, to moisten [?] / of שד השמן. The meaning is the warm moisture in which the life of man abides; also in the droughts of summer, by way of parable: the moisture dries up and his days draw near to death."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {1 "The phrase לשד השמן is textually uncertain; translated hyper-literally as it stands in the witness."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:10.826975954Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}